# 19. IMPORTANT ENGINEERING RULES

Follow these instructions throughout development.

1. Never build a static mockup and claim it is a working application.
2. Never use hardcoded data where real user data should be displayed.
3. Never create buttons that do not perform their stated action.
4. Never put secrets or API keys in frontend code.
5. Never create an agent that has no clearly defined responsibility.
6. Never allow agents to modify unrelated user data.
7. Never fabricate job listings or external data.
8. Never claim that AI-generated scores guarantee employment.
9. Use structured schemas and predictable contracts.
10. Make components reusable.
11. Keep frontend and backend business logic separate.
12. Preserve working functionality when introducing new features.
13. Test code after making significant changes.
14. Explain any manual configuration required.
15. Keep the project ready for GitHub export and external development.
16. Prioritize actual working end-to-end workflows over unnecessary complexity.
17. Use sample data only when clearly identified as sample data.
18. Explain errors honestly and fix them rather than hiding them.
19. Keep architecture, database and code documentation updated.
20. Never claim that ProofPath is 100% production-ready without appropriate testing.

